From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pkgconfig: make gstdxstream.pc prefix relocatable

The build installs the plugin into a DESTDIR staging tree and then builds the
custom_library/postprocess_library/* projects against it, pointing pkg-config
at that tree:

    DESTDIR="$S/install" meson install
    export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$S/install/usr/lib/pkgconfig:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH"

meson's pkgconfig module always writes the absolute install prefix, so the
staged gstdxstream.pc says `prefix=/usr`. That is right for the installed
target copy and wrong for this staged one, and pkg-config does not correct it:
PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR is only applied to .pc files found underneath the
sysroot, and this one is deliberately outside it. The postprocess libraries
were therefore handed literal host paths:

    pkg-config --cflags gstdxstream  ->  -I/usr/include
    pkg-config --libs   gstdxstream  ->  -L/usr/lib/gstreamer-1.0 -lgstdxstream

while the sibling gstreamer-1.0 flags in the same invocation were correctly
rewritten into the sysroot, which is what makes the asymmetry visible in
meson-log.txt.

The -I is caught by gcc and is fatal when the toolchain is built with
--enable-poison-system-directories, as OpenEmbedded's is:

    cc1plus: error: include location "/usr/include" is unsafe for
        cross-compilation [-Werror=poison-system-directories]

The -L is the more dangerous half and is silent: it puts the build host's
library directory on the search path of a cross link. It resolves correctly
today only because the caller happens to pass an explicit -L into the staging
tree first.

Emit the .pc from a template so prefix can be written relative to ${pcfiledir}.
The .pc lives in <prefix>/lib/pkgconfig, so ${pcfiledir}/../.. is <prefix> in
both cases: $S/install/usr while cross-compiling, /usr once installed on the
target. No consumer needs to change, and the generated target .pc is
byte-equivalent in meaning to the previous one.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/gst-dxstream-plugin/src/meson.build
+++ b/gst-dxstream-plugin/src/meson.build
@@ -125,17 +125,21 @@
   )
 endif
 
-# Generate pkg-config file
-pkg = import('pkgconfig')
-pkg.generate(
-    gstdxstream,
-    name: 'gstdxstream',
-    filebase: 'gstdxstream',
-    description: 'DeepX Stream GStreamer Plugin',
-    requires: ['gstreamer-1.0 >= 1.0'],
-    variables: [
-        'plugindir=' + '${libdir}' / 'gstreamer-1.0'
-    ],
+# Generate pkg-config file.
+#
+# Written from a template rather than via the pkgconfig module so that `prefix`
+# can be expressed relative to ${pcfiledir}. The module always emits the
+# absolute install prefix (/usr), which is correct on the target but wrong while
+# cross-compiling: the custom_library/ postprocess libraries consume this .pc
+# out of a DESTDIR staging tree, and an absolute /usr made pkg-config hand them
+# -I/usr/include and -L/usr/lib/gstreamer-1.0 -- host paths. A ${pcfiledir}
+# relative prefix resolves correctly in both places.
+pkg_conf = configuration_data()
+pkg_conf.set('VERSION', meson.project_version())
+configure_file(
+    input: 'gstdxstream.pc.in',
+    output: 'gstdxstream.pc',
+    configuration: pkg_conf,
     # Install to lib/pkgconfig (standard location, not lib/arch/pkgconfig!)
     install_dir: join_paths(get_option('prefix'), 'lib', 'pkgconfig')
 )
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gst-dxstream-plugin/src/gstdxstream.pc.in
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+prefix=${pcfiledir}/../..
+includedir=${prefix}/include
+libdir=${prefix}/lib
+
+plugindir=${libdir}/gstreamer-1.0
+
+Name: gstdxstream
+Description: DeepX Stream GStreamer Plugin
+Version: @VERSION@
+Requires: gstreamer-1.0 >=  1.0
+Libs: -L${libdir}/gstreamer-1.0 -lgstdxstream
+Cflags: -I${includedir}
-- 
2.43.0

